[0.002, "o", "\u001b[4;35mGoal\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                 \r\n\r\nCreate the secrets and host prerequisites the loop must not create. Wait until this fragment's deps are done (human fragments reach you before their \r\ndeps finish); the vault key names come from \u001b[1;36;40mdocs/plans/runner-fleet.md\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/runner_fleet.ts\u001b[0m on \u001b[1;36;40mtools\u001b[0m.                               \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mSteps\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                \r\n\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0mProxmox: create a role limited to what the runner models call (VM allocate, config, power, snapshot, SDN and firewall on the runner pool,         \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mdatastore space on the runner storage), a \u001b[1;36;40mrunner-fleet@pve\u001b[0m user and an API token for it with privilege separation. Put the token into the Swamp   \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mvaul"]
[0.000, "o", "t of the Spark collector user under the key names the design lists.                                                                           \r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0mSpark: generate the dispatch SSH key for the user the design names (\u001b[1;36;40mssh-keygen -t ed25519\u001b[0m), store the private key path and the pinned host keys in\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mthe vault; keep the public key for the image recipes' placeholder.                                                                                \r\n\u001b[36m 3 \u001b[0mMac mini: create the runner host user, authorize the dispatch key for it, install Tart if the inventory said it is missing, and record its host   \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mkey in the vault.                                                                                                                                 \r\n\u001b[36m 4 \u001b[0mWindows: put the licence or product key in the vault under the design's key name, if the edition needs one.                                       \r\n\u001b[36m 5 \u001b[0mRun \u001b[1;36;40mswamp vault list-keys\u001b[0m (or the curren"]
[0.000, "o", "t equivalent from \u001b[1;36;40mswamp help vault\u001b[0m) as the collector user and confirm every key name the design lists is  \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mpresent.                                                                                                                                          \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mResolve with\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                         \r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36;40mloopq resolve <this id> --done --note \"<step 5 output: key names only, no values>\"\u001b[0m                                                                   \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mAcceptance\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                           \r\n\r\nEvery key name listed in the design is present in the collector vault; no value appears in the note or any repository file.                          \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mOperator decision (2026-09-26)\u001b[0m                                                   "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                    \r\n\r\nOperator decision 2026-09-26 (see tb-0075). Also on the laptop: create a standard (non-admin) macOS user for the runner; enable Remote Login for that\r\nuser only; add the Spark dispatch public key to its \u001b[1;36;40mauthorized_keys\u001b[0m with \u001b[1;36;40mfrom=\"<spark address>\",restrict,port-forwarding,permitopen=\"192.168.64.*:22\"\u001b[0m\r\n(confirm the Tart NAT subnet with \u001b[1;36;40mtart ip\u001b[0m on a running VM); install Tart system-wide from an admin account (\u001b[1;36;40mbrew install cirruslabs/cli/tart\u001b[0m). On the\r\nMac mini: macOS version (\u001b[1;36;40msw_vers\u001b[0m, Tart needs 13 or later), free disk (\u001b[1;36;40mdf -h /\u001b[0m, about 100 GB needed), install Tart the same way. Paste the laptop and \r\nMac mini checks into the note, without addresses.                                                                                                    \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1mhistory\u001b[0m \u001b[92m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[1mWhen\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mEvent\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mTo\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mBy\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m \u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mDetail\u001b[0m\r\n───────────────────────────────\r\n"]
